-- title:
--   Divisibility of Pic⁰ of a curve over an algebraically closed field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero and let $F$ be a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, subject to two hypotheses: first, `hfg`, that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ and $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$; second, `IsCurveOver K F`, which asserts that (i) every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor, i.e. a finitely supported function $D$ on the set of places with $D(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ for all $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, (ii) each residue field $v.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is a finite $K$-module, and (iii) the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, divisors are finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on places, and $\mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$ is the group of divisors of degree zero modulo the subgroup of principal divisors of degree zero. Then for every natural number $n \neq 0$ and every class $x \in \mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$ there exists $y \in \mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$ with $n \cdot y = x$; that is, $\mathrm{Pic}^0(K,F)$ is a divisible group.
--
--   Classically this is the surjectivity of multiplication by $n$ on the points of the Jacobian of a smooth projective curve over an algebraically closed field, the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ being the group of $K$-points of the Jacobian. It is used in the parts of the development that study the $n$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and reductions of curves, for instance in comparing torsion subgroups under component charts and constant reductions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_exists_nsmul_eq.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_nsmul_eq (K F : Type*) [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F]
    [IsAlgClosed K] [CharZero K]
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental K x ∧ FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F)
    [IsCurveOver K F]
    (n : ℕ) (hn : n ≠ 0) (x : Pic0 K F) :
    ∃ y : Pic0 K F, n • y = x := by sorry
